<title>SPAIN: France Telecom gets 16 bln pta syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>France Telecom gets 16 bln pta syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French telecommunications firm France Telecom received a syndicated loan of 16 billion pesetas, Spain's saving bank association CECA said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CECA is acting as lead manager while SBC Warburg structured the loan.</p>
<p>The 10-year loan pays six-month peseta Libor plus 0.35 percent, with a maximum of 8.05 percent.</p>
<p>Nineteen savings bank were part of the deal.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
